response:
Of course!  Loops are used to repeatedly execute a block of code as long as a certain condition is true.  For example, you might use a loop to make an infinite number of "Rock, Paper, Scissors" games, like this:

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    move(playerOne, computerOne);
    move(playerOne, computerTwo);
    move(playerTwo, computerOne);
    move(playerTwo, computerTwo);
}

where n is the number of games to be played.  The "move" function performs the action to be taken when a particular number of the possible outcomes is selected as the result of the game.

